+# Restricted Organon reproduction
+
+Both versions retain model-authored search plugins. V1 exposes custom scheduling, parent selection and survival functions. V2 adds a one-candidate direction and a dynamic direction function. Both versions share the same Worker, model route, tool permissions, evaluator, and input construction. Start each comparison from a fresh copy of the same task with matching model settings and budget.
+
+## Modifier tools
+
+- `evolve_status` exposes the task statement, official candidate history, active hooks and remaining budget.
+- `evolve_inspect` exposes the task program and evaluator entry point or a recorded candidate's source and public evaluation JSON. The files are read-only. Post-run private evaluation stays outside the search session.
+- `evolve_define` takes `name`, `purpose`, and `host_code`. Pass an existing `plugin_id` to create a new version. `evolve_activate` starts a chosen version and `evolve_deactivate` restores the previous provider. `evolve_plugins` shows the active hooks. Changes take effect between `evolve_run` chunks.
+
+## JavaScript hook contract
+
+The source body returns an object exporting any subset of the permitted functions. Each function receives a private JSON snapshot with `history`, `alive`, `budget`, `k`, and `maxPopulation`. The host performs candidate allocation, Worker invocation, scoring, history recording and budget enforcement.
+
+One VM context stays live for each activated plugin version in a task run. Module variables are shared across that plugin's hooks and persist across candidate iterations and `evolve_run` chunks. Each synchronous call has a 250 ms limit and receives two additional fields:
+
+- `state.turn` is the zero-based call index of the current hook in this activation. To refer to the total number of candidate slots used, use `state.budget.used`.
+- `state.memory` starts as an empty JSON object and is shared by all hooks in the same plugin. Write durable counters, cursors, or other small state into this object. Successful hook calls checkpoint it alongside their turn counters in `run/search-policy.json`. The hook result and memory share a 65,536-character JSON limit.
+
+On process restart the plugin code initializes a new VM context. Its checkpointed `turn` and `memory` are available on the first call. Activating a different version or deactivating the plugin discards the replaced activation's state. Activating the already active version preserves it.
+
+| Function | Contract |
+| --- | --- |
+| `*loop(state)` | Drive the search chunk by yielding fixed operations. Choose when to select, generate, evaluate, and update the population. Each yield receives the corresponding operation result. Return to end the chunk. |
+| `loop(state)` | Compatibility mode. Return one or more parent plans or `null` to delegate to selection. Runs the default generate, evaluate and threshold-triggered survival cycle. |
+| `select(state)` | Return a primary ID or `{parent_id, donors}`. Custom selectors can select any recorded or pending generated candidate. The default upstream fitness-proportional selector samples the alive population. |
+| `survive(state)` | Return the IDs that should be alive. A custom hook can reactivate any previously evaluated candidate. The default is upstream top-k on the alive population. |
+| `guidance(state)` | V2 only. Return a direction for the current candidate, or an empty string. The input additionally supplies `primary` metadata and the selected `donors`. |
+
+The generator receives current history, pending candidates, the global budget and the remaining candidate slots in this chunk. Generate and evaluate can be interleaved freely. The fixed Worker runs once on generation and uses one candidate slot. An evaluation uses the fixed judge and records its official fitness. Requesting evaluation for an already scored ID returns its existing result. Unevaluated candidates remain pending across chunks, including after the generation budget is exhausted. Generator mode does not trigger automatic survival at the default threshold.
+
+```js
+return {
+  *loop(state) {
+    if (state.remaining < 2) return
+    const parent = state.history[0].id
+    const a = yield { op: 'generate', parent_id: parent }
+    const b = yield { op: 'generate', parent_id: parent }
+    yield { op: 'evaluate', id: b.id }
+    yield { op: 'evaluate', id: a.id }
+    yield { op: 'set_population', ids: [parent, a.id, b.id] }
+  }
+}
+```
+
+The full operation set is `{op:'state'}`, `{op:'select'}`, `{op:'generate',parent_id,donors?}`, `{op:'evaluate',id}`, `{op:'survive'}` and `{op:'set_population',ids}`. `survive` calls the active survival policy. `set_population` updates membership directly using evaluated IDs, including archived candidates. Operations are executed one at a time.
+
+The Worker starts from the primary parent's workspace. A fixed prompt builder adds the nominated donors' IDs, any official fitness and program text as reference data. Donors are optional and distinct from one another and from the primary. To override dynamic guidance on one candidate in V2, call `evolve_set_guidance`. That text is consumed after candidate allocation and Worker execution. The dynamic hook supplies guidance again for the following candidate. The default Worker persona and task instructions remain the base prompt. The Worker uses the same confined file tools across variants.
+
+`run/search-policy.json` records the source code, versions, active hooks, fixed model settings and changes. `run/population.jsonl` records the primary parent, donors, supplied guidance and official fitness. The VM interface passes data only. Run the harness in the dedicated experiment environment for guest-code isolation at the process and OS level.
+
+## Launch
+
+Use the Linux and Docker dependencies from the author kit. `bash setup.sh` installs the restricted evolve-loop from the current source and the original candidate-builder archive with DeepSeek Harness `dsh-v0.1.7-rc.1`.
+
+From the DSH checkout, after setup:
+
+```bash
+export ORGANON_VARIANT=v1
+export ORGANON_BUDGET=5
+PATH="$DSH_HOME/benchmarks/venv/bin:$PATH" pnpm dsh web --no-open
+```
+
+Run V2 with `ORGANON_VARIANT=v2` and a separate task copy. Start an **Evolve Mode** session in the task directory and send [PROMPT.restricted.md](PROMPT.restricted.md). Use `node --test plugins/dsh-evolve-loop/tests/restricted.node.mjs` for the dependency-free tests, which use a stub Worker and evaluator subprocess.
